            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Human Rights and Racial Justice</strong><br>\nEleanor was vocal in her support for civil rights and worked against racial discrimination. She was a part of the NAACP and advocated for anti-lynching laws. Her stance on racial equality was ahead of her time, and she used her influence to promote equal rights for all Americans.</p>\n\n<p><strong>International Diplomacy</strong><br>\nAfter World War II, Eleanor Roosevelt was appointed as a delegate to the United Nations by President Harry S. Truman. She played a crucial role in drafting the Universal Declaration of Human Rights, believing that human rights were the cornerstone of peace and justice.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Advocacy for Women</strong><br>\nEleanor used her platform to champion women's rights both domestically and internationally. She encouraged women to participate in all aspects of life, from work to politics, and worked tirelessly to break down the barriers they faced.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
